[0.025, "o", "\u001b[2;1H\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;168;162;154;49m· Welcome to saya. Type a message and press Enter. Type / for commands, Tab to accept a suggestion, ↑/↓ for history,\u001b[3;1H· Alt+Enter for a newline, Ctrl+C to quit.\u001b[4;1H· Mode: accept-edits — workspace file writes run unasked; every other call still asks. Plan still denies writes under\u001b[5;1H· `bypass`\u001b[5;43H\u001b[23m\u001b[39;49m                                     \u001b[7;1HYOU\u001b[7;23H                                                                            \u001b[8;1H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;106;155;204;49m  Build me a small browser game called Neon Snake in this empty folder. It should be a self-contained HTML5 canvas game\u001b[9;1H  with just index.html and game.js: arrow keys steer a glowing snake, eating orbs grows it and adds score, the snake\u001b[10;1H  speeds up as the score climbs, and hitting a wall or yourself shows a game-over screen with a restart key. Make it\u001b[11;1H  look neon and fun. Add a small test suite for the game logic using Node's built-in test runner (node --test) and run\u001b[12;1H  "]
