[0.062, "o", "\u001b[2;1H                                                                                                                    \u001b[2;120H║\u001b[3;1HYOU                                       \u001b[3;120H║\u001b[4;1H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;106;155;204;49m  Build me a small browser game called Neon Snake in this empty folder. It should be a self-contained HTML5 canvas game\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;157;139;245;49m█\u001b[5;1H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;106;155;204;49m  with just index.html and game.js: arrow keys steer a glowing snake, eating orbs grows it and adds score, the snake\u001b[5;120H\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;157;139;245;49m█\u001b[6;1H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;106;155;204;49m  speeds up as the score climbs, and hitting a wall or yourself shows a game-over screen with a restart key. Make it\u001b[6;120H\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;157;139;245;49m█\u001b[7;1H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;106;155;204;49m  look neon and fun. Add a small test suite for the game logic using Node's built-in test runner (node --test) and run\u001b[7;120H\u001b[22m\u001b[38;2;157;139;245;49m█\u001b[8;3H\u001b[1m\u001b[38;2;106;155;204;49mit until\u001b[8;12Hit p\u001b[8;17Hsses. Finish by\u001b[8;33Hte\u001b[8;37Hin"]
